[h1]Languages[/h1][url=https://lyuwenhan.github.io/extensions/minecraft-java/data/assets/infinity-fireworks/README/README.html]EN/English[/url] | [url=https://lyuwenhan.github.io/extensions/minecraft-java/data/assets/infinity-fireworks/README/README_ZH-CN.html]ZH-CN/简体中文[/url]
[h1]Infinity Fireworks[/h1]Fabric mod for Minecraft that lets firework rockets be used without consuming the item stack.
[h2]Features[/h2][list]
[*]Firework rockets are not consumed when launched from a block[/*]
[*]Firework rockets are not consumed when used for elytra boosting[/*]
[*]Works in singleplayer through the integrated server[/*]
[*]Works on Fabric servers when installed server-side[/*]
[*]Keeps vanilla firework behavior, including flight data and explosions[/*]
[*]No commands or configuration required[/*]
[/list][h2]Usage Example[/h2][code]Use a firework rocket -> rocket launches -> item count stays the same[/code]
Field description:
[list]
[*][b]Use a firework rocket[/b] - Right-click a block or boost while gliding[/*]
[*][b]rocket launches[/b] - Vanilla firework behavior still happens[/*]
[*][b]item count stays the same[/b] - The stack is not decremented[/*]
[/list][h2]Behavior[/h2][list]
[*]Applies to all firework rockets, including customized rockets[/*]
[*]Does not create new items or change crafting recipes[/*]
[*]Does not affect dispenser behavior[/*]
[*]Creative mode behavior remains unchanged[/*]
[/list][h2]Multiplayer Safety[/h2][list]
[*]Client-only installation does not change item consumption on remote servers[/*]
[*]Multiplayer servers must install the mod server-side for the effect to apply[/*]
[*]When installed on a server, the non-consumption behavior applies to players using that server[/*]
[*]The mod does not register commands or send custom gameplay packets[/*]
[/list][h2]Supported Versions[/h2][list]
[*]Minecraft 1.21.11[/*]
[*]Fabric Loader 0.18+[/*]
[*]Fabric API[/*]
[*]Java 21[/*]
[/list][h2]License[/h2]MIT
